Z||000009||lou_dias||12-12-2001||12:24 PM||||I finally got to play a Cube Sunday, Madden 2002 actually, it was awesome to look at but I miss the arcade feel of the older ones.  Atleast it played more realistically than NFL Fever on the XBOX.  By that I simply mean that on NFL Fever, my friend threw to the same receiver with the same play for about 400 yards worth and 200 to the other.  Well, needless to say, Madden is a superior football game to NFL Fever.<P>Comparing the graphics, I would say they are atleast equal but Madden has some nice camera motion on the close-ups.<P>This isn't a good comparison since I'd really like to see Madden on both systems side by side.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BN Boomer||12-12-2001||01:02 PM||||After the debate about various consoles in the other thread and <I>some</I> people claiming that the Xbox crashes all of the time, it's kind of ironic that the first incident of failure reported here involved a GameCube. Sorry, Squoach, I know that doesn't help you out and it's maddening when you buy something that doesn't seem to work correctly. At least it looks like it just turned out to be just a bad disc than a problem with your system. Glad to see you got it worked out.<P>I don't play or buy the pro-sports type of games, so I wouldn't know anything about Madden 2002 or NFL Fever. After Christmas I'll let you know how MX2002 compares between the Xbox and PlayStation2, though. I guess I wont be able to compare Halo or Project Gotham Racing to any other system. Most of the titles I've seen for GameCube just don't appeal to me since I'm buying the Xbox for the older kids and the younger ones can keep playing Mario games on the N64.||||reg||1
