Z||000012||BN Boomer||12-13-2001||03:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lou_dias:<BR><B>actually Nintendo is targeting all markets judging from all the blood in Tony Hawk.  Also Resident Evil won't have any shortage either.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Which probably explains why I didn't say something to the effect that Nintendo is targeting the GameCube <I>exclusively</I> towards younger kids. It just appears to me that <I>most</I> of their games are aimed at that particular market segment.<P>Frankly, I don't care about blood and gore myself. If that's your cup of tea, I guess it's a good thing that Nintendo's GameCube can at least somewhat satiate that need.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||lou_dias||12-13-2001||09:18 AM||||I agree that most of there games are for kids, but what is it that attracts/classifys games for adults?<P>it's bloody violence and sex<P>that makes Tetris a kid's game even though adults can enjoy it.<P>it's just a classification...<P>anyway, I'm glad Nintendo is not limiting creativity on there hardware...and should not be classified as solely a "kid's" game machine.||||reg||1
